# Next.js regenerates this per-command and its contents differ between
# `next dev` and `next build`. The stable half lives in
# apps/conditional-immortality/types/next-env.d.ts, which is committed.
#
# Anchored to the one path Next generates. Written bare as `next-env.d.ts` it
# matched at every depth, which silently ignored the committed replacement too.
/apps/conditional-immortality/next-env.d.ts

# The animations.dev installer writes the same twelve skills into a directory
# for every agent it finds on the machine. Claude Code's copy is committed, in
# .claude/skills/, because that is what this repository is developed with. The
# rest stay local: they work exactly the same from disk, and four more copies of
# the same files would be noise in a repository about theology.
/.cursor/
/.codex/
/.opencode/
/.gemini/
